-- Rust binding for anthill.prelude.PartialEq's own `neq`. Proposal 038.
--
-- `neq` is keyed to the SPEC op: the host function negates `semantic_equal`, which finds
-- the head carrier's own `eq` from the value before deciding anything structurally.
--
-- `eq` has no host implementation here. Each scalar carrier maps its own member
-- (`Int64.eq` in `int64.anthill`, `Float.eq` in `float.anthill`, …), a sort writes its
-- own, and a call that reaches the spec operation with no member — one no type reaches,
-- or one at a composite with no `eq` of its own — is compared by its values in the
-- interpreter (`eval::builtins::builtin_eq`) as the resolver's `SemEq` compares the goal.
--
-- A spec-level mapping does NOT certify any carrier of `PartialEq` (WI-876 / WI-931,
-- `typing::op_backed`).
namespace anthill.prelude
  provides PartialEq language rust
    artifact "rustland/anthill-core/src/eval/builtins.rs"
    operation_map {
      neq: "partial_eq_neq"
    }
  end
end
